   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 425 of the laws of 2012, incorporating the\nMain-Transit Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association and\nproviding for its powers and duties, in relation to the Main-Transit Volunteer\nFire Department Benevolent Association's purpose and the use of foreign fire\ninsurance premium taxes",
    "basePrintNo": "S8835",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8835-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 3 & 7, Chap 425 of 2012",
    "lawSection": "Volunteer Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8835\n\nSPONSOR: RATH\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 425 of the laws of 2012, incorporating the Main-\nTransit Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association and\nproviding for its powers and duties, in relation to the Main-Transit\nVolunteer Fire Department Benevolent Association's purpose and the use\nof foreign fire insurance premium taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis legislation would amend chapter 425 of the laws of 2012 to allow\nthe Main-Transit Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association\nto use the foreign fire insurance premium taxes for the purpose of\nenhancing morale by providing social and recreational activities for its\nvolunteer members, who are indigent, disabled or injured in the perform-\nance of their duties, and their families, and to also promote the volun-\nteer fire service within the territory protected by the Main-Transit\nFire Department. This bill also changes the name of the benevolent asso-\nciation to the \"Main-Transit Volunteer Fire Department Benevolent Asso-\nciation\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends sections 1 to change the name of the Association to the\nMain-Transit Volunteer Fire Department Benevolent Association, section 3\nto amend the purposes of the Main-Transit Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's\nBenevolent Association, and section 7 to update references to the Insur-\nance Law.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Main-Transit Volun-\nteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent Association and the Main-Transit\nFire Department. In order to enhance the goals of the Association, it is\nnecessary to amend chapter 425 of the Laws of 2012 to take out language\nthat limits the use of the foreign fire insurance premium taxes received\nby the Association.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided however that the amend-\nments to section 7 of chapter 425 of the Laws of 2012 relating to incor-\nporating the Main-Transit Volunteer Exempt Firefighter's Benevolent\nAssociation made by section one of this act shall apply to taxes due on\npremiums received on and after January 1, 2022.\n",
